Z||000000||shain||07-10-2000||05:31 AM||||just when i start to iron all the bugs out of my 2m4......<BR>i step out of my car @ work, and all i can smell is gas!! Friggin great!! my gas line is leaking!! <P>anyhow... i was aboot to replace the affected area with a small piece of hose by cuting the old line stretching it over the old line and putting 2 clamps on it. <BR>please tell me that this is cool to do, and i dont have to replace the whole line.<P>it seems like it should be alright but i would like to hear what you guys (and chicks too) have to say! thanx<P>-----<BR>shain<BR>85 2m4<BR>gettin 1 mile per gal!! ||||reg||8
Z||000001||batboy||07-10-2000||07:22 AM||||If just the end is bad, you can cut it off and reinstall it, if you have enough slack in the line. If you have to "stretch" the hose to make it fit, then it's too short. You probably should replace the whole line, if the end is bad, the rest of the hose probably ain't great either. BTW, the topic title is probably not a good choice...you risk offending some folks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||07-10-2000||11:38 AM||||Like me.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Cliff Pennock||07-10-2000||12:23 PM||||Yes, it is a bit offending to some people. Therefor I have changed the title.<p>[This message has been edited by Cliff Pennock (edited 07-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||shain||07-11-2000||04:37 AM||||GEE WHIZZ BEAVE!!  lighten up. i dont want to get into a religious debate on here i just want to find out how  to fix my gas line!<P>anyways,batboy, the fuel line is not made out of rubber hose its made out of metal. thats why its leaking cause its rusted through. i was asking if its cool to put a small peice of hose in place of the rusted out part.<BR>ppllleeeeeassse someone tell me<BR>GOOD or BAD!!!?||||reg||1
Z||000005||ChadMan||07-11-2000||10:14 AM||||You've got a 4-banger, right?  The TBI fuel lines only carry about 15 psi of pressure.  You can buy reinforced rubber gas lines at most hardware stores and I think you'd be OK patching your line with that.  Just be sure and buy some extra hose and make sure you've got plenty of overlap on both ends between the metal and the rubber and clamp it down really good with hose clamps.<P>I'd be a little afraid of a patch like this on a V6, since its fuel lines carry around 45 psi.||||reg||1
Z||000006||lennyb4||07-11-2000||10:22 AM||||Chadmans right. I replaced 90% of my fuel line with neopreme hose and havent had a problem since. Just be careful to tie it back (zip strips work great) away from any exaust or other area's that may get hot. Neopreme hose is good for pressure systems but will still burn through over time. Local autopart stores carry it for around .86* to $1.00 per foot.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Cliff Pennock||07-11-2000||12:02 PM||||Shain, it's got nothing to do with people needing to lighten up. It's a simple question of having a little respect for those who might get offended. That's all. But like I said, I changed the title so no harm done.||||reg||1
